-- title:
--   Exactly q+1 components through a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Fixed are a prime $q\ge 5$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$.
--
--   **Coefficient field and function field.** $L$ is a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` asks for a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. $K$ is an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and `hK` pins it down as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79): that is, $K$ is generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the Laurent series belonging to the function field of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H$ with modulus $(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H=$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` is the kernel of a unit-reduction map on $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times$.
--
--   **The base ring.** $A$ is a domain which is a discrete valuation ring, henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field; `hAq` requires $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and `hξA` that $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$. $K$ carries an $A$-algebra structure compatible with that of $L$. The element $j\in K$ is required by `hj` to have Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the coefficientwise image in $L$ of the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function, and to be non-zero. Further, $\varpi\in A$ generates $\mathfrak m_A$, and $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (a tame root of $q$).
--
--   Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ (the $j$-finite chart algebra), `jChartFin A ↥K j` for $j$ viewed in $C$, and $\mathfrak X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model, the pushout of the two maps $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the middle chart algebra to $\operatorname{Spec}C$ and to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j^{-1}$-chart algebra, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A$.
--
--   **The supersingular point.** $y$ is a maximal ideal of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$, and `hss` requires: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **The global chart hypothesis `hArig`.** For every point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ equal to the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` and lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ with `ιFin`-image $z$ at which the supersingularity condition of the previous paragraph holds for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there exist: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e\colon \widehat{\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v-f\,u\big),$$
--   subject to a conjunction of seven riders, formulated in terms of the completion map $\mathrm{toC}$ from the stalk to its adic completion, the quotient map $\mathrm{mkS}$, and the germ homomorphism $\mathrm{germY}\colon C\to\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ obtained from the affine identification of the `ιFin`-chart: (i) $e$ carries the germ of $a\in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) (the condition that $\tau$ realises on $q$-expansions the action of the matrix `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` on ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H$, read through any $\iota$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$), $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ and such $\tau$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; (iv) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and such $\tau$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ transporting the action of $\tau$ through $e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$, $\theta$ fixing the classes of constants, $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (v) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting the class of $X_0$ or the class of $X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing an element of the shape $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h_i$ with $h_i\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then $P_1$ and $P_2$ have distinct contractions along $e\circ\mathrm{toC}$; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ with the same two conditions and with tangent direction $(1,0)$, an element $a\in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $(q\ell)$-fold expansion of the $j$-expansion) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0\in A$ with the difference of this element and $a_0$ in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0\ge 1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W$ whenever $a$ or $b$ is a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, and such that $e$ sends the germ of that difference to the class of $h$.
--
--   **The chosen point and the chosen chart.** Then $z,\varpi_z$ with `hϖz`, `hz`, and $y'$ with `hy'`, `hss'` are fixed as above, together with `hy'y`: $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$. Fixed as well are a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1\colon A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk at $z$ with $S:=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts, for this datum, exactly the conjunction of the seven riders (i)–(vii) listed above.
--
--   **The centre, the blow-up algebra and the valuation ring.** The ideal $J\subseteq C$ is pinned down by `hJ` as the infimum of the set of those ideals $J'$ for which there are $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and an $L$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt … γ⁻¹ K τ` and preserving $C$, with $J'$ the preimage under the induced endomorphism of $C$ of the contraction along $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. The subalgebra $B\subseteq K$ over $A$ is pinned down by `hB` as the $C$-subalgebra generated by $\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}$, i.e. $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$. Finally $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ with `hBW`: $B\subseteq W$.
--
--   The remaining hypotheses are grouped as follows. `hR1`: $C\subseteq B$, and every element of $K$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne 0$. `hR2`: $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses): an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $W$ and in $\mathfrak m_W$; and $f\in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$. `hEQ` (five clauses): first, for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho\colon B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by $\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}-1$) whose kernel consists of the elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$, which is compatible with $A\to k$ via the residue map, and which is equivariant in the following sense: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt … γ⁻¹ K τ` and preserving $W$, there is a unit $c$ of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) such that $\rho\circ\tau=\mathrm{hAction}(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)\circ\rho$ on $B$, and $c\ne 1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; second, such $\tau$ preserve $B$; third, every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$ arises from some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and some such $\tau$ in the sense that $\tau$ carries every element of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$ into $Q$; fourth, an element of $B$ all of whose translates by such pairs $(\gamma,\tau)$ lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by the image of $\varpi$; fifth, for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ as above, if $\tau$ preserves $y$ on $C$ then $\tau$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a finite set `comps` of ideals of $C=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` such that an ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $C$ belongs to `comps` if and only if $\mathfrak p$ is prime, contains the image of $\varpi$, is contained in $y$ and is different from $y$; and the cardinality of `comps` is $q+1$.
--
--   Thus the primes of the $j$-finite chart algebra which lie over $\varpi$ and are strictly contained in the supersingular maximal ideal $y$ form a finite set with exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   The $q+1$ primes produced here are the generic points of the components of the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart passing through the supersingular point $y$, the Igusa components of the reduction at a supersingular point; they correspond to the $q+1$ branches of the completed Drinfeld chart, one for each $\mathbb F_q$-rational line, via [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.branchPrimes_of_sub_drinfeldForm_mem_pow`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.branchPrimes_of_sub_drinfeldForm_mem_pow). The statement is used in the construction of the set of ends of the chart and of the Igusa-type valuation subrings attached to them, by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_finset_ends_iff_isLocalization_blowupChart_card_eq_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_finset_ends_iff_isLocalization_blowupChart_card_eq_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_igusaType_valuationSubring_not_le_end_of_end_blowupChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_igusaType_valuationSubring_not_le_end_of_end_blowupChart).
